ReplicateLayer[3] makes three copies of the whole vector (3\[Times]P), which \
is not what we want.", "Text"], 
  Cell[
   "{Dimensions[ReplicateLayer[3][fB]], Dimensions[ReplicateLayer[3, \
2][fB]]}", "Input", CellLabel -> "In[18]:="], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"3", ",", "3"}], 
          "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"3", ",", "3"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]], 
   "Output", CellLabel -> "Out[18]="], Cell["8. The message on every edge", 
   "Section"], Cell[TextData[{"Times, second use (mB, mN): the replicated \
scalars are multiplied by the unit vectors, giving the force vector ", 
     Cell[BoxData[SubscriptBox["m", "p"]]], " = ", 
     Cell[BoxData[SubscriptBox["f", "p"]]], " ", 
     Cell[BoxData[SubscriptBox["u", "p"]]], 
     " that edge p exerts on its first bead."}], "Text"], 
  Cell["mB = times[{rep[fB], uB}];\n{MatrixForm[mB], MatrixForm[fB uB]}", 
