branch, with the cutoff, and a Plus at the end. Apart from the sizes, this is \
exactly BuildForceNet in PolymerNN.wl.", "Text"], 
  Cell["forceNet[phiBond_, phiPair_] := NetGraph[<|\n    \"phiB\" -> \
NetMapOperator[phiBond], \"phiN\" -> NetMapOperator[phiPair], \"cut\" -> \
ThreadingLayer[Times],\n    \"repB\" -> ReplicateLayer[3, 2], \"repN\" -> \
ReplicateLayer[3, 2],\n    \"mB\" -> ThreadingLayer[Times], \"mN\" -> \
ThreadingLayer[Times],\n    \"Ab\" -> NetArrayLayer[\"Array\" -> Ab, \
LearningRateMultipliers -> 0],\n    \"An\" -> NetArrayLayer[\"Array\" -> An, \
LearningRateMultipliers -> 0],\n    \"sumB\" -> DotLayer[], \"sumN\" -> \
DotLayer[], \"total\" -> ThreadingLayer[Plus]|>,\n   {NetPort[\"bf\"] -> \
\"phiB\" -> \"repB\", {\"repB\", NetPort[\"bu\"]} -> \"mB\", {\"Ab\", \"mB\"} \
-> \"sumB\",\n    NetPort[\"nf\"] -> \"phiN\", {\"phiN\", NetPort[\"nc\"]} -> \
\"cut\" -> \"repN\",\n    {\"repN\", NetPort[\"nu\"]} -> \"mN\", {\"An\", \
\"mN\"} -> \"sumN\", {\"sumB\", \"sumN\"} -> \"total\" -> NetPort[\"F\"]},\n  \
 \"bf\" -> {3, 4}, \"bu\" -> {3, 3}, \"nf\" -> {3, 4}, \"nu\" -> {3, 3}, \
\"nc\" -> 3];\nfullNet = forceNet[phi, phi]", "Input", 
   CellLabel -> "In[26]:="], 
